{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-355378",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the largest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that largest output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the smallest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that smallest output occurs.\n\nHere, the outputs are $-8,$ $1,$ $3,$ and $10.$ \n\n- The largest output is $10,$ and it occurs at $x=2.$\n\n- The smallest output is $-8,$ and it occurs at $x=4.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{x\\in S}f(x) & =10 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x) & =2 \\\\ {min}_{x\\in S}f(x) & =-8 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x) & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
